SysResEval for Debian
=====================

Installing from the apt repository
----------------------------------
The packages of the GitHub releases are served, signed, by the apt repository of the project
(<dist> is trixie or forky):

  sudo curl -fsSL -o /usr/share/keyrings/sysreseval-archive-keyring.gpg \
      https://sysreseval.github.io/sysreseval/apt/sysreseval-archive-keyring.gpg
  sudo curl -fsSL -o /etc/apt/sources.list.d/sysreseval.sources \
      https://sysreseval.github.io/sysreseval/apt/sysreseval-<dist>.sources
  sudo apt update && sudo apt install sysreseval

The web site
------------
sysreseval-web (the portal, on any host: no Docker needed) and sysreseval-agent (on every pool
host, next to sysreseval) make the web site of the project: the students work from a browser on
projects running on the pool.  Both units are disabled by default; copy and edit the examples
of /usr/share/doc/sysreseval-web/examples/web.toml (root:sre-web 0640, like the web.d/*.toml
files it may import) and
/usr/share/doc/sysreseval-agent/examples/agent.toml (root 0600) to /etc/sysreseval/, then
`systemctl enable --now sysreseval-web` / `sysreseval-agent`.  The reverse proxy examples
sre-web-nginx.conf and sre-web-apache.conf (this one authenticates the users against the LDAP
directory itself) are next to web.toml.  See the "Web site" page of the documentation.

The Display tab of the web site (the graphical applications of the labs, e.g. Wireshark) needs
tigervnc-standalone-server and openbox on the pool hosts (Recommends of sysreseval-agent) and
`[display] enabled = true` in agent.toml; the X processes run as the sreweb-x11 user the
package creates.

Layout of the package
---------------------
  /usr/sbin/sre                          command-line interface (run by root, or by the students
                                         through /usr/bin/sre-wrapper and the sudoers rule)
  /usr/bin/sysreseval                    graphical interface of the students and instructors
  /usr/bin/sre-wrapper                   what the GUI and the students call: sudo /usr/sbin/sre --user
  /usr/lib/sysreseval/                   the Python code; lib/ (grading helpers) is readable by the
                                         sre user only
  /usr/share/sysreseval/lab/sre/         the labs of the package (readable by the sre user only)
  /var/lib/sre/                          projects, archives, exam.json, home/ (the directories
                                         shared with the machines), lab/ (the lab directory:
                                         lab/sre is a link to the labs above, add the site's own
                                         labs next to it, e.g. /var/lib/sre/lab/s4/tp_ssh/srelab.py)
  /etc/sysreseval/params.py              site parameters (see below)
  /etc/sudoers.d/sysreseval              the rule that lets every user run `sre --user` as root:
                                         restrict it to the students' group on a shared host
  /usr/lib/systemd/system/sysreseval-preload-images.service
                                         pre-pulls the Docker images at boot; disabled by default

Site parameters
---------------
The parameters of /usr/lib/sysreseval/SRE/params.py are the defaults; /etc/sysreseval/params.py
(a conffile, Python syntax) sets the values of this host: the groups allowed to run the archive
tools (admin_gids), the terminal emulator of the GUI (terminal_cmd_prefix), whether privileged
machines are allowed, where the archives go...  The file lists them.  Do not edit params.py
itself: it is replaced at every upgrade.

The sre user
------------
The package creates the system user `sre` (dynamic uid) and adds it to the `docker` group.  When
/var/lib/sre or the archives are shared over NFS between hosts, create the user yourself before
installing the package, with the same uid everywhere; the package keeps an existing user.

After the installation
----------------------
1. Labs with 'switch' or 'managed' networks need the Kathara network plugin that knows the
   switch types: run `sysreseval-network-plugin` once per Docker host (as root, with the Docker
   daemon running and network access).
2. The machines of the labs display their graphical programs on the X server of the host, which
   must accept TCP connections on port 6000 (GDM: DisallowTCP=false, LightDM:
   xserver-allow-tcp=true); see the installation guide of sysreseval-doc.
3. `sre update` is disabled: the package is updated with apt.
4. Removing the package keeps /var/lib/sre (projects, archives, site labs) and the sre user;
   `apt purge` removes only the empty directories and /etc/sysreseval.
